Figure 5 demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and uptake by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Compared to soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvanted OVA, Nano-11 formulated OVA results in a higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA within cells and a greater percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) containing OVA in the draining lymph nodes on both day 1 and day 2 post-injection. This enhanced and targeted antigen delivery to immunopotentiating MigDCs underscores Nano-11's superior adjuvant capability, contributing to a more effective immune response.